IMPORT prelude

-- Carriage by Air (Montreal Convention, 1999) Act 2007 (Singapore) -- what a passenger or shipper can claim from an airline:
-- whether the Convention applies (Art 1; s 3), the carrier's liability and the limits for death or injury, delay, baggage and cargo
-- (Arts 17 to 22, with the Schedule's three Addenda), when lost baggage or cargo may be claimed for (Arts 13(3), 17(3)), the written
-- complaint deadlines (Art 31; s 8), the two-year bar and contribution claims (Art 35; s 9), costs after a written offer (Art 22(6)),
-- non-compensatory damages (Art 29), clauses that vary the limits (Arts 25, 26, 49) and where an action may be brought (Art 33).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation, version
-- in force from 28/12/2024, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CAMC1999A2007.txt. The latest amendment annotated is the
-- Third Addendum to the Schedule, "[S 1006/2024 wef 28/12/2024]". SECTION NUMBERS FOLLOW THE BODY: the arrangement of sections at
-- the top of the deposit is one place out of step (it lists "1." with no title and numbers Short title as 2).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0101 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The
-- answer is almost all in the Convention set out in the Schedule, which s 3(1) gives the force of law. SCOPED to the claims a
-- passenger or a cargo shipper makes. Not encoded: documentation (Arts 3 to 11), the right of disposition and delivery of cargo
-- beyond Art 13(3) (Arts 12 to 16), contributory negligence (Art 20), conversion into Singapore dollars (Art 23), review of limits
-- (Art 24; s 7), advance payments (Art 28), servants and agents (Arts 30, 43) beyond s 9(1), successive and actual carriers (Arts 36,
-- 39 to 48), arbitration (Art 34), insurance (Art 50; s 10), the Minister's powers (ss 11, 12, 13) and the final clauses.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Carriage by Air (Montreal Convention, 1999) Act 2007 -- claims against the carrier`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` a b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `s 3 and Article 1 -- when the Convention governs`

-- s 3(1): the Convention, so far as it relates to "the rights and liabilities of carriers ... passengers, consignors, consignees and
-- other persons", has "the force of law in Singapore in relation to any carriage by air to which the Convention applies regardless of
-- the nationality of the aircraft". (2): it "does not affect rights or liabilities arising out of an occurrence before 16 November
-- 2007". Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD.
GIVEN `the date of the occurrence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act governs the occurrence` IF `the date of the occurrence` AT LEAST 20071116

-- Art 1(1): the Convention "applies to all international carriage of persons, baggage or cargo performed by aircraft for reward. It
-- applies equally to gratuitous carriage by aircraft performed by an air transport undertaking." (2): international carriage is
-- carriage where, by the agreement, departure and destination are "within the territories of two States Parties, or within the
-- territory of a single State Party if there is an agreed stopping place within the territory of another State, even if that State is
-- not a State Party". Carriage within one State Party without such a stop "is not international carriage".
-- (The deposit does not list which States are Parties, so the journeys below are described abstractly.)
DECLARE Journey IS ONE OF
    `from one State Party to another`
    `a return trip within one State Party with an agreed stop in a non-party State`
    `a domestic flight within one State Party`
    `from a State Party to a non-party State`
    `a return trip within a non-party State with an agreed stop in a State Party`

GIVEN `the journey` IS A Journey
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the journey is international carriage` IF
    CONSIDER `the journey`
    WHEN `from one State Party to another` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a return trip within one State Party with an agreed stop in a non-party State` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the journey` IS A Journey, `for reward` IS A BOOLEAN, `by an air transport undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Convention applies` IF
    `the journey is international carriage` `the journey` AND (`for reward` OR `by an air transport undertaking`)

§§ `Articles 21 and 22 and the Addenda -- the limits in Special Drawing Rights`

-- Art 21(1): 100,000 SDR for each passenger; Art 22(1) delay: 4,150 SDR; 22(2) baggage: 1,000 SDR for each passenger; 22(3) cargo:
-- 17 SDR per kilogramme. Revised by the Addenda "with effect from" 30 December 2009 (113,100 / 4,694 / 1,131 / 19), 28 December
-- 2019 (128,821 / 5,346 / 1,288 / 22, [S 734/2019]) and 28 December 2024 (151,880 / 6,303 / 1,519 / 26, [S 1006/2024]).
-- INFERENCE: the Addenda say from when the revised limits take effect, not whether that is measured at the date of the occurrence,
-- of the contract or of judgment. This encoding keys them to a single "relevant date" and leaves the choice to the caller.
DECLARE Limit IS ONE OF
    `the Article 21 threshold for death or injury`
    `the delay limit per passenger`
    `the baggage limit per passenger`
    `the cargo limit per kilogramme`

GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A NUMBER, `original` IS A NUMBER, `from 2009` IS A NUMBER, `from 2019` IS A NUMBER, `from 2024` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the figure in force` MEANS
    IF `the relevant date` AT LEAST 20241228 THEN `from 2024`
    ELSE IF `the relevant date` AT LEAST 20191228 THEN `from 2019`
         ELSE IF `the relevant date` AT LEAST 20091230 THEN `from 2009`
              ELSE `original`

GIVEN `the limit` IS A Limit, `the relevant date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the limit in SDR` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `the Article 21 threshold for death or injury` THEN `the figure in force` `the relevant date` 100000 113100 128821 151880
    WHEN `the delay limit per passenger` THEN `the figure in force` `the relevant date` 4150 4694 5346 6303
    WHEN `the baggage limit per passenger` THEN `the figure in force` `the relevant date` 1000 1131 1288 1519
    WHEN `the cargo limit per kilogramme` THEN `the figure in force` `the relevant date` 17 19 22 26

§§ `Articles 17(1) and 21 -- death or bodily injury`

-- Art 17(1): the carrier "is liable for damage sustained in case of death or bodily injury of a passenger upon condition only that the
-- accident which caused the death or injury took place on board the aircraft or in the course of any of the operations of embarking or
-- disembarking". Art 21(1): up to the threshold "the carrier shall not be able to exclude or limit its liability". (2): it is not
-- liable for damages "to the extent that they exceed" the threshold "if the carrier proves that: (a) such damage was not due to the
-- negligence or other wrongful act or omission of the carrier or its servants or agents; or (b) such damage was solely due to the
-- negligence or other wrongful act or omission of a third party". There is NO upper limit otherwise.
-- (Art 20 exoneration for the claimant's own negligence is not modelled.)
GIVEN `the accident was on board or while embarking or disembarking` IS A BOOLEAN, `the damages proved` IS A NUMBER,
      `the relevant date` IS A NUMBER, `the carrier proves it was not negligent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the carrier proves a third party was solely to blame` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the carrier's liability for death or injury` MEANS
    IF NOT `the accident was on board or while embarking or disembarking` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the carrier proves it was not negligent` OR `the carrier proves a third party was solely to blame`
         THEN `the smaller of` `the damages proved` (`the limit in SDR` `the Article 21 threshold for death or injury` `the relevant date`)
         ELSE `the damages proved`

§§ `Articles 19 and 22(1), (5) -- delay of passengers`

-- Art 19: the carrier "is liable for damage occasioned by delay"; but not "if it proves that it and its servants and agents took all
-- measures that could reasonably be required to avoid the damage or that it was impossible for it or them to take such measures".
-- Art 22(1): for each passenger the liability is limited to the delay limit. 22(5): paragraphs 1 and 2 "shall not apply if it is
-- proved that the damage resulted from an act or omission of the carrier, its servants or agents, done with intent to cause damage or
-- recklessly and with knowledge that damage would probably result".
GIVEN `the damages proved` IS A NUMBER, `the relevant date` IS A NUMBER,
      `the carrier proves it took all reasonable measures` IS A BOOLEAN, `intent or recklessness is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the carrier's liability for passenger delay` MEANS
    IF `the carrier proves it took all reasonable measures` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `intent or recklessness is proved` THEN `the damages proved`
         ELSE `the smaller of` `the damages proved` (`the limit in SDR` `the delay limit per passenger` `the relevant date`)

§§ `Articles 17(2) and 22(2), (5) -- baggage`

-- Art 17(2): checked baggage -- liable "upon condition only that the event which caused the destruction, loss or damage took place on
-- board the aircraft or during any period within which the checked baggage was in the charge of the carrier. However, the carrier is
-- not liable if and to the extent that the damage resulted from the inherent defect, quality or vice of the baggage. In the case of
-- unchecked baggage, including personal items, the carrier is liable if the damage resulted from its fault or that of its servants or
-- agents."
DECLARE Bag IS ONE OF
    `checked baggage`
    `unchecked baggage`

GIVEN `the bag` IS A Bag, `the event was on board or while the carrier had charge of it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the damage came from an inherent defect of the bag` IS A BOOLEAN, `the carrier or its people were at fault` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier is liable for the baggage` IF
    CONSIDER `the bag`
    WHEN `checked baggage` THEN `the event was on board or while the carrier had charge of it`
                                AND (NOT `the damage came from an inherent defect of the bag`)
    WHEN `unchecked baggage` THEN `the carrier or its people were at fault`

-- Art 22(2): limited to the baggage limit "for each passenger unless the passenger has made, at the time when the checked baggage was
-- handed over to the carrier, a special declaration of interest in delivery at destination and has paid a supplementary sum if the case
-- so requires. In that case the carrier will be liable to pay a sum not exceeding the declared sum, unless it proves that the sum is
-- greater than the passenger's actual interest in delivery at destination." 22(5) lifts the limit for intent or recklessness.
-- A declared sum of 0 means no declaration. INFERENCE: where the carrier proves the declared sum exceeds the actual interest, the cap
-- becomes the actual interest (the text says only that the declared-sum cap then does not hold).
GIVEN `the damages proved` IS A NUMBER, `the relevant date` IS A NUMBER, `the declared sum` IS A NUMBER,
      `the carrier proves the declared sum exceeds the actual interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `the actual interest` IS A NUMBER,
      `intent or recklessness is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the carrier's liability for baggage` MEANS
    IF `intent or recklessness is proved` THEN `the damages proved`
    ELSE IF `the declared sum` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN `the smaller of` `the damages proved`
                  (IF `the carrier proves the declared sum exceeds the actual interest` THEN `the actual interest` ELSE `the declared sum`)
         ELSE `the smaller of` `the damages proved` (`the limit in SDR` `the baggage limit per passenger` `the relevant date`)

-- Art 17(3): "If the carrier admits the loss of the checked baggage, or if the checked baggage has not arrived at the expiration of
-- twenty-one days after the date on which it ought to have arrived, the passenger is entitled to enforce against the carrier the rights
-- which flow from the contract of carriage." Art 13(3) is the same for cargo with "seven days". Art 52: "days" are calendar days.
-- INFERENCE: "at the expiration of" 21 days is read as at least 21 whole days having passed.
GIVEN `the carrier admits the loss` IS A BOOLEAN, `days overdue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the passenger may claim the checked baggage as lost` IF
    `the carrier admits the loss` OR `days overdue` AT LEAST 21

GIVEN `the carrier admits the loss` IS A BOOLEAN, `days overdue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignee may claim the cargo as lost` IF
    `the carrier admits the loss` OR `days overdue` AT LEAST 7

§§ `Articles 18 and 22(3), (4) -- cargo`

-- Art 18(1): liable for destruction, loss or damage to cargo "upon condition only that the event ... took place during the carriage
-- by air" (the period the cargo is in the carrier's charge, (3)). (2): not liable "if and to the extent it proves" the damage resulted
-- from "(a) inherent defect, quality or vice of that cargo; (b) defective packing of that cargo performed by a person other than the
-- carrier or its servants or agents; (c) an act of war or an armed conflict; (d) an act of public authority carried out in connection
-- with the entry, exit or transit of the cargo".
DECLARE CargoCause IS ONE OF
    `an inherent defect of the cargo`
    `bad packing by the shipper`
    `bad packing by the carrier`
    `an act of war`
    `a customs seizure on entry`
    `rough handling by the carrier`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A CargoCause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the carrier has an Article 18(2) defence` IF
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `an inherent defect of the cargo` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `bad packing by the shipper` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an act of war` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a customs seizure on entry` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Art 22(4): for part of the cargo, "the weight to be taken into consideration ... shall be only the total weight of the package or
-- packages concerned. Nevertheless, when the destruction, loss, damage or delay of a part of the cargo ... affects the value of other
-- packages covered by the same air waybill ... the total weight of such package or packages shall also be taken into consideration".
GIVEN `weight of the packages concerned` IS A NUMBER, `weight of other packages on the waybill` IS A NUMBER,
      `their value is affected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weight that counts` MEANS
    IF `their value is affected` THEN `weight of the packages concerned` PLUS `weight of other packages on the waybill`
    ELSE `weight of the packages concerned`

-- Art 22(3): limited to the cargo limit per kilogramme "unless the consignor has made ... a special declaration of interest in
-- delivery at destination" (same declared-sum rule as baggage). Art 22(5) lifts ONLY "paragraphs 1 and 2": the cargo limit holds
-- even where the carrier acted with intent or recklessly. The parameter is taken so that the cases can show it has no effect.
GIVEN `the damages proved` IS A NUMBER, `the relevant date` IS A NUMBER, `the kilogrammes` IS A NUMBER, `the declared sum` IS A NUMBER,
      `the carrier proves the declared sum exceeds the actual interest` IS A BOOLEAN, `the actual interest` IS A NUMBER,
      `intent or recklessness is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the carrier's liability for cargo` MEANS
    IF `the declared sum` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the smaller of` `the damages proved`
             (IF `the carrier proves the declared sum exceeds the actual interest` THEN `the actual interest` ELSE `the declared sum`)
    ELSE `the smaller of` `the damages proved` (`the kilogrammes` TIMES `the limit in SDR` `the cargo limit per kilogramme` `the relevant date`)

§§ `Article 31 and s 8 -- written complaints`

-- Art 31(2): "In the case of damage, the person entitled to delivery must complain to the carrier forthwith after the discovery of the
-- damage, and, at the latest, within seven days from the date of receipt in the case of checked baggage and fourteen days from the date
-- of receipt in the case of cargo. In the case of delay, the complaint must be made at the latest within twenty-one days from the date on
-- which the baggage or cargo have been placed at his or her disposal." (3): "Every complaint must be made in writing". (4): "If no
-- complaint is made within the times aforesaid, no action shall lie against the carrier, save in the case of fraud on its part."
-- s 8: in Art 31(2) "damage" includes "loss of part of the baggage or cargo", and receipt means "receipt of the remainder of it".
-- Art 31 sets no complaint period for a TOTAL loss (the two-year bar in Art 35 still applies).
DECLARE Problem IS ONE OF
    `damage to checked baggage`
    `part of the checked baggage missing`
    `damage to cargo`
    `part of the cargo missing`
    `delay of baggage`
    `delay of cargo`
    `checked baggage never delivered`

GIVEN `the problem` IS A Problem
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Article 31 requires a complaint` IF
    CONSIDER `the problem`
    WHEN `checked baggage never delivered` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the problem` IS A Problem
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the latest day for the complaint` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the problem`
    WHEN `damage to checked baggage` THEN 7
    WHEN `part of the checked baggage missing` THEN 7
    WHEN `damage to cargo` THEN 14
    WHEN `part of the cargo missing` THEN 14
    WHEN `delay of baggage` THEN 21
    WHEN `delay of cargo` THEN 21
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the problem` IS A Problem, `days after receipt or disposal` IS A NUMBER, `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `fraud by the carrier` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action can lie despite Article 31` IF
        (NOT `Article 31 requires a complaint` `the problem`)
    OR  `fraud by the carrier`
    OR  (`in writing` AND `days after receipt or disposal` AT MOST `the latest day for the complaint` `the problem`)

§§ `Article 35 and s 9 -- time for bringing proceedings`

-- Art 35(1): "The right to damages shall be extinguished if an action is not brought within a period of two years, reckoned from the
-- date of arrival at the destination, or from the date on which the aircraft ought to have arrived, or from the date on which the
-- carriage stopped." (2): the method of calculating is for the law of the court. s 9(1): the same two years for an action against the
-- carrier's servant or agent acting within the scope of employment. s 9(4): "action" includes arbitration.
-- Counted here in whole months.
GIVEN `months since arrival, due arrival or stop` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the right to damages is extinguished` IF `months since arrival, due arrival or stop` GREATER THAN 24

-- s 9(2): Art 35 is not to be read "as applying to any proceedings for contribution between persons liable". (3): subject to ss 4 and
-- 29 of the Limitation Act 1959 (not modelled), contribution must not be sought "after the expiration of 2 years from the time when a
-- court gives judgment or makes an award against the person seeking to recover the contribution".
GIVEN `months since the judgment or award against the claimant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contribution claim is barred` IF `months since the judgment or award against the claimant` GREATER THAN 24

§§ `Article 22(6) -- costs on top of the limits`

-- Art 22(6): the limits "shall not prevent the court from awarding, in accordance with its own law, in addition, the whole or part of
-- the court costs and of the other expenses of the litigation incurred by the plaintiff, including interest. The foregoing provision
-- shall not apply if the amount of the damages awarded ... does not exceed the sum which the carrier has offered in writing to the
-- plaintiff within a period of six months from the date of the occurrence causing the damage, or before the commencement of the action,
-- if that is later." Times in months from the occurrence; an offer amount of 0 means no written offer.
GIVEN `the written offer` IS A NUMBER, `month of the offer` IS A NUMBER, `month the action began` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offer counts` IF
    `the written offer` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (`month of the offer` AT MOST 6 OR `month of the offer` LESS THAN `month the action began`)

GIVEN `the damages awarded` IS A NUMBER, `the written offer` IS A NUMBER, `month of the offer` IS A NUMBER,
      `month the action began` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may add costs and interest above the limit` IF
    NOT (`the offer counts` `the written offer` `month of the offer` `month the action began`
         AND `the damages awarded` AT MOST `the written offer`)

§§ `Article 29 -- what kind of damages`

-- Art 29: any action for damages, "however founded, whether under this Convention or in contract or in tort or otherwise, can only be
-- brought subject to the conditions and such limits of liability as are set out in this Convention ... In any such action, punitive,
-- exemplary or any other non-compensatory damages shall not be recoverable."
DECLARE DamagesHead IS ONE OF
    `compensatory damages`
    `punitive damages`
    `exemplary damages`

GIVEN `the head` IS A DamagesHead
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the damages are recoverable` IF
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `compensatory damages` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Articles 25, 26 and 49 -- clauses in the ticket or waybill`

-- Art 25: "A carrier may stipulate that the contract of carriage shall be subject to higher limits of liability than those provided for
-- in this Convention or to no limits of liability whatsoever." Art 26: "Any provision tending to relieve the carrier of liability or to
-- fix a lower limit ... shall be null and void, but the nullity of any such provision does not involve the nullity of the whole
-- contract". Art 49: clauses agreed "before the damage occurred" that infringe the rules "whether by deciding the law to be applied, or
-- by altering the rules as to jurisdiction, shall be null and void".
DECLARE Clause IS ONE OF
    `a higher limit`
    `no limit at all`
    `a lower limit`
    `no liability for delay`
    `a choice of some other law`
    `a forum not allowed by Article 33`

GIVEN `the clause` IS A Clause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause is valid` IF
    CONSIDER `the clause`
    WHEN `a higher limit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no limit at all` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Article 33 -- where to sue`

-- Art 33(1): an action "must be brought, at the option of the plaintiff, in the territory of one of the States Parties, either before
-- the court of the domicile of the carrier or of its principal place of business, or where it has a place of business through which the
-- contract has been made or before the court at the place of destination." (2): for death or injury also in the State Party where
-- "at the time of the accident the passenger has his or her principal and permanent residence and to or from which the carrier operates
-- services for the carriage of passengers by air ... and in which that carrier conducts its business of carriage of passengers by air
-- from premises leased or owned by the carrier itself or by another carrier with which it has a commercial agreement". (3)(b):
-- nationality "shall not be the determining factor". The place of departure, as such, is not on the list.
DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the carrier's domicile`
    `the carrier's principal place of business`
    `the carrier's place of business through which the contract was made`
    `the place of destination`
    `the passenger's principal and permanent residence`
    `the place of departure`
    `the passenger's State of nationality`

GIVEN `the forum` IS A Forum, `in a State Party` IS A BOOLEAN, `a death or injury claim` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the carrier flies there and does business from premises there` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an action may be brought there` IF
    `in a State Party` AND
        (CONSIDER `the forum`
         WHEN `the carrier's domicile` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the carrier's principal place of business` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the carrier's place of business through which the contract was made` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the place of destination` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the passenger's principal and permanent residence`
              THEN `a death or injury claim` AND `the carrier flies there and does business from premises there`
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
